   268	In Figure 2, you can see a classic example of a probabilistic model,
   269	namely a linear model, where the uni-variate data _𝑦_ is believed to
   270	have a noisy linear relationship with the input values _𝑥_ . The variables _𝑦_ _𝑖_ are constrained to observed data and we are interested in
